        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold mb-6">
          What to ask for before you trust a polyphenol number
        </h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed mb-8" style="opacity: 0.8;">
          Seven items. A producer who can supply all seven is making a checkable
          statement; one who can supply two is making an advertisement.
        </p>
        <ol class="space-y-4">
          {[
            ["The method, named.", "IOC chromatographic, qNMR or Folin-Ciocalteu. Without it the figure has no units anyone can interpret."],
            ["The laboratory, named.", "A result with no laboratory behind it cannot be queried or repeated."],
            ["Accreditation.", "ISO/IEC 17025 covers testing competence. IOC recognition covers olive oil specifically. ISO 9001 is a management standard and says nothing about the assay."],
            ["The harvest year.", "Phenolic content is a function of harvest timing and declines from pressing onward."],
            ["The sample date.", "The gap between pressing and analysis is part of what the number means."],
            ["The compound breakdown.", "Oleocanthal and oleacein individually, in mg/kg. A total alone hides the distribution."],
            ["The certificate itself.", "Openable, in full, including the uncertainty and the limits of quantification."],
          ].map(([title, body], i) => (
            <li class="flex gap-4">
              <span
                class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold"
                style={`background-color: ${GREEN}; color: ${CREAM};`}
